{
  "format": "owa-conformance-v1",
  "specVersion": "owa.dev/v1",
  "operation": "blob",
  "notes": [
    "Every input.manifest must pass metadata-only validation before the boundary operation. These are not tests that validateManifest reads blob content.",
    "oci-write: input.blobs maps declared digest to actual base64 source bytes, then writeOciLayout is invoked.",
    "oci-read: materialize input.layoutFiles verbatim beneath a fresh directory and invoke readOciLayout. The layout is static, independently encoded, and deliberately inconsistent only at the boundary named by the vector.",
    "The write size-mismatch sample intentionally has both wrong length and digest: the existing write boundary checks size first. Read content-size sample has the correct digest but manifest and layer both declare size 4 for the 3-byte blob.",
    "Success checks artifact identity and exact returned blob bytes. Failure checks only the stable errorCategory, never human-readable messages. No S3 behavior is changed or assumed.",
    "oci-read layouts carry the transport descriptor representation: each layer mediaType is the RFC 6838 type/subtype of the OWA file mediaType (parameters such as \"; charset=utf-8\" removed; a value that is not a valid type/subtype becomes application/octet-stream), while the config blob keeps the full OWA mediaType. The reader requires that mapped value; a layer carrying the parameterized or a different media type is rejected. See docs/oci.md.",
    "Duplicate content (issue #9): blob-write-duplicate-content and blob-read-duplicate-content are the portable anchors for several file entries sharing one content digest. One OCI layer descriptor exists per file entry, identified by dev.openwebartifact.path; repeated descriptors reference the same blob digest, whose bytes appear once in input.blobs / the layout and once in expected.blobs; the config keeps each entry's full OWA mediaType while descriptors carry the mapped per-entry type; descriptor order is not file order.",
    "Index reference selection (issue #36): readOciLayout selects the index.json descriptor whose annotations carry org.opencontainers.image.ref.name as a string exactly equal to the requested ref, and requires exactly ONE such descriptor: zero matches and duplicate matches both fail, descriptor order never breaks a tie, a missing annotations object, missing key, null, number, boolean, empty or different string never matches, and requesting latest does NOT fall back to manifests[0]. blob-read-index-exact-ref-selection is the portable success anchor: its index lists a complete decoy artifact under ref v1 FIRST and the expected artifact under latest SECOND, so a first-descriptor or positional reader imports the wrong artifact. Selection failures are transport-local OCI layout errors without a portable OWA errorCategory, so they are pinned by direct tests in both implementations rather than by negative vectors. See docs/oci.md."
  ],
